<header>
  <h1>Undo in a Shared Graph</h1>
  <p>A command-line tool that keeps a graph in one SQLite file and can take back a subtree delete after other people and an ingest job have kept working on the same graph. This page covers the parts of the tool, how the graph sits in SQLite, and how undo decides what to bring back.</p>
</header>

<section>
  <h2><span class="n">1</span>Architecture</h2>
  <p>There are no services to run. The task fixes the tool to one process and one database file, so the picture is one Python program with a few parts inside it, one SQLite file next to it, and two small helper programs outside it.</p>

